<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The player's on-screen controls, as a sibling of the navigation shell rather than a page in its
  frame: the pane and the header must not stay on screen behind a film.

  Everything here is drawn over a transparent island with mpv's child HWND showing through it. That
  is what fact 1 in HostWindow's remarks bought, and it is why this file replaces the WinForms
  shell's five hand-painted layered top-level windows (PlayerBar 1291 lines, PlayerFlyout 813,
  VolumeRail 283, SkipSectionButton 205, Chrome 696) with declarative XAML in one visual tree. The
  four consequences worth naming:

    * Requirement 1, resizing. Nine SetWindowPos calls per WM_SIZE became one MoveAndResize for the
      island plus one for the video child. The chrome resizes because it is laid out, not moved.
    * Requirement 12, the mess when switching episodes. The island is above the video by
      construction, so nothing has to be brought to the front and the handover cover cannot lose a
      z-order race it used to lose.
    * Requirements 9/10/11, the reveal rule. Real pointer events arrive here, so ChromeReveal is
      driven one event at a time instead of off a 40 ms Cursor.Position poll.
    * The pickers. MenuFlyout gets a genuine DesktopAcrylicBackdrop from the framework's own
      generic.xaml, keyboard navigation and narrator names, none of which PlayerFlyout had.

  No transitions and no fades on the two overlays the pointer's own bands reveal: requirement 9 was
  「不要淡入淡出了，鼠标移动到对应位置直接显示」, so the transport bar and the title strip are Visibility
  flips. The volume rail is the exception the user asked for afterwards —
  「加大音量条的尺寸，显示方式改为淡入淡出，鼠标指针越接近右边的中心显示越明显」 — and it fades through an
  implicit ScalarTransition on its own Opacity, explained where it is declared. The one storyboard in
  the file is PulseBadge's, which nobody reveals — it is the one-second 暂停/播放 acknowledgement the
  user asked to have an animation, and it explains itself down there.

  Every readout here is bound to PlayerViewModel with x:Bind rather than assigned from code-behind —
  the clock, the seek and volume sliders, the play glyph, the source line, the skip offer, the chapter
  peek and the handover cover — and the transport buttons are Command bindings. What is left as a
  Click= or an Opened= handler is there because it is a WinUI behaviour rather than player state: the
  window commands, the fullscreen and 置顶 toggles, the six menus (whose rows are built on open), the
  seek track's own size and hover, and the mute button, which flashes the volume rail as well as
  muting. Visibility on Bar/TitleStrip/ThinLine and the rail's Opacity stay code-owned for the same
  reason: they are the reveal rule's output, not a property of what is playing.

  The scrims are gradients rather than an in-app AcrylicBrush, and deliberately. WinUI 3 has no
  host-backdrop acrylic, so an AcrylicBrush here would sample the transparent island above the video
  rather than the picture, and blur nothing — it would come out a flat tint pretending to be a
  material. A gradient is also simply the better answer over arbitrary video: acrylic's luminosity
  tint washes out over a bright frame, and a scrim that fades to nothing keeps the picture readable
  right up to the controls.
-->
<UserControl
    x:Class="EmbyNian.Shell.Views.PlayerPage"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:local="using:EmbyNian.Shell.Views"
    xmlns:vm="using:EmbyNian.Shell.ViewModels"
    xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
    xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
    mc:Ignorable="d"
    RequestedTheme="Dark"
    FontFamily="{StaticResource EgUiFontFamily}"
    FontSize="{StaticResource EgBodyFontSize}"
    IsTabStop="True"
    UseSystemFocusVisuals="False"
    Visibility="Collapsed">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <!-- Turns the slider's own 0..1000 into a clock, which is what makes hovering the seek bar
             say 「1:07:32」 for free. A stateful converter because the duration is the file's, not the
             slider's; the page keeps it current. -->
        <local:SeekClockConverter x:Key="SeekClockConverter" />

        <!-- Flat, borderless and see-through until pointed at: over a picture, a button's own filled
             background is more visible than its glyph and reads as a panel rather than a control. -->
        <Style x:Key="OsdButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FFF2F4F7" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10,6" />
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="40" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource EgUiFontFamily}" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="OsdGlyphStyle" TargetType="FontIcon">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="16" />
        </Style>

        <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="BottomScrim" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
            <GradientStop Offset="0.0" Color="#000C0E11" />
            <GradientStop Offset="0.35" Color="#8C0C0E11" />
            <GradientStop Offset="1.0" Color="#F00C0E11" />
        </LinearGradientBrush>

        <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="TopScrim" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
            <GradientStop Offset="0.0" Color="#E60C0E11" />
            <GradientStop Offset="1.0" Color="#000C0E11" />
        </LinearGradientBrush>

        <!-- 章节刻度. A brush rather than a colour per tick: the marks are rebuilt on every resize and
             on every chapter list, and a hundred brushes for a hundred chapters is a hundred more
             composition objects than the picture needs. -->
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ChapterTickBrush" Color="#B3FFFFFF" />

        <!-- The 暂停/播放 badge's one second, and the only storyboard in the file — see PulseBadge for
             why this one is not the fade the reveal rule refuses.

             Held together rather than split in two because the pause pulse and the resume pulse are the
             same gesture with a different glyph; the page sets the glyph and begins this. Opacity is up
             within 90 ms so the acknowledgement is immediate, holds while it is read, and is gone by
             1000 ms; the scale starts small and ends slightly over, so it grows on arrival and drifts
             outward as it goes rather than shrinking back into nothing — a badge that retreated the way
             it came would read as being cancelled rather than acknowledged.

             Opacity and scale are both composition properties, so this runs off the UI thread and needs
             no EnableDependentAnimation. Completed collapses the badge: left visible at zero opacity it
             would still be a hit-test-free but laid-out element on every subsequent frame. -->
        <Storyboard x:Key="PulseStoryboard" Completed="OnPulseCompleted">
            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames
                Storyboard.TargetName="PulseBadge"
                Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0" Value="0" />
                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.09" Value="1" />
                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.62" Value="1" />
                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:1" Value="0" />
            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames
                Storyboard.TargetName="PulseScale"
                Storyboard.TargetProperty="ScaleX">
                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0" Value="0.72" />
                <SplineDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.22" KeySpline="0.1,0.9 0.2,1" Value="1" />
                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:1" Value="1.18" />
            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames
                Storyboard.TargetName="PulseScale"
                Storyboard.TargetProperty="ScaleY">
                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0" Value="0.72" />
                <SplineDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.22" KeySpline="0.1,0.9 0.2,1" Value="1" />
                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:1" Value="1.18" />
            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
        </Storyboard>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <!-- Transparent, not null: a null background is not hit-testable, and every pointer event the
         reveal rule runs on lands on this grid. It is also what lets the video show through. -->
    <Grid x:Name="Root" Background="Transparent" SizeChanged="OnRootResized">

        <!-- ================= 右键画面菜单 =================
             The tree is PlayerMenuCatalog's, harvested from the bundled input.conf's own uosc menu, so
             「右键 → 画面 → 开/关 裁切填充」 is where someone who has used that configuration expects it.
             Built on first open rather than in XAML because it is a hundred-odd rows of data, and as a
             ContextFlyout rather than a RightTapped handler so the menu key and Shift+F10 reach it too. -->
        <Grid.ContextFlyout>
            <MenuFlyout x:Name="PictureMenu" Opening="OnPictureMenuOpening" />
        </Grid.ContextFlyout>

        <!-- ================= 顶部：标题与窗口操作 =================
             The three window commands are the last column rather than a separate overlay of the shell's,
             and that is the whole of 「全屏后右上角的图标不会自动隐藏，鼠标移到左上角时会跟置顶跟统计重叠」:
             an overlay outside this strip could neither come and go with the reveal rule nor be kept out
             of 统计/置顶's corner, and it did both wrong at once. As a column it hides with the strip and
             the grid guarantees no two of them can ever share a pixel.

             The strip pads only its left edge, so those buttons reach the top-right corner the way every
             other window's do; everything else in the row carries its own top inset instead. -->
        <Grid
            x:Name="TitleStrip"
            Height="96"
            VerticalAlignment="Top"
            Background="{StaticResource TopScrim}"
            Padding="16,0,0,0"
            ColumnSpacing="8"
            Visibility="Collapsed">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

            <Button
                x:Name="BackButton"
                Command="{x:Bind ViewModel.StopCommand}"
                Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}"
                VerticalAlignment="Top"
                Margin="0,10,0,0"
                ToolTipService.ToolTip="返回（Esc）">
                <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE72B;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
            </Button>

            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="4,12,0,0">
                <TextBlock
                    x:Name="TitleText"
                    FontSize="{StaticResource EgTitleFontSize}"
                    FontWeight="SemiBold"
                    MaxLines="1"
                    Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Title, Mode=OneWay}"
                    TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                <TextBlock
                    x:Name="SubtitleText"
                    FontSize="{StaticResource EgCaptionFontSize}"
                    Foreground="#FFA5ADBA"
                    MaxLines="1"
                    Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Subtitle, Mode=OneWay}"
                    TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                    Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.SubtitleVisibility, Mode=OneWay}" />
            </StackPanel>

            <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Top" Spacing="2" Margin="0,10,0,0">
                <!-- 需求 7：字幕字体. A search box rather than a menu of families: there are a few thousand of
                     them on a machine with fonts installed, and no flyout that long is navigable. The rows
                     are drawn in the family they offer, same as the 设置 card's list.

                     The text is the search, not the value — taking the keyboard clears it and opens the
                     whole list, and leaving puts the family currently in use back. The current family also
                     stays in the list whatever is typed (SettingFontRow.Refilter has the why), so a search
                     that matches nothing still has one row; Resolve is what keeps Enter from picking it by
                     accident.

                     Everything the box does to the rest of the player is in PlayerPage.Fonts.cs: it pins the
                     chrome while it has focus, and it silences the player's single-letter keys — F, M, N, P
                     and Space are all commands and all letters a font name is spelled with. -->
                <AutoSuggestBox
                    x:Name="FontBox"
                    Width="188"
                    Margin="0,0,6,0"
                    VerticalAlignment="Top"
                    GotFocus="OnFontBoxFocus"
                    ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.SubtitleFont.Matches, Mode=OneWay}"
                    KeyDown="OnFontBoxKeyDown"
                    LostFocus="OnFontBoxBlur"
                    PlaceholderText="字幕字体"
                    QuerySubmitted="OnFontQuerySubmitted"
                    SuggestionChosen="OnFontSuggestionChosen"
                    TextChanged="OnFontBoxTextChanged"
                    TextMemberPath="Name"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="字幕字体：输入任意一段名字搜索，回车或点一下就换，正在播的片子立刻生效">
                    <AutoSuggestBox.QueryIcon>
                        <SymbolIcon Symbol="Find" />
                    </AutoSuggestBox.QueryIcon>
                    <AutoSuggestBox.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:FontOption">
                            <StackPanel Padding="0,2,0,2">
                                <TextBlock
                                    FontFamily="{x:Bind Preview}"
                                    FontSize="15"
                                    Text="{x:Bind Name}"
                                    TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                <TextBlock
                                    FontFamily="{x:Bind Preview}"
                                    FontSize="12"
                                    Opacity="0.7"
                                    Text="{x:Bind Localized}"
                                    TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                    Visibility="{x:Bind LocalizedVisibility}" />
                            </StackPanel>
                        </DataTemplate>
                    </AutoSuggestBox.ItemTemplate>
                </AutoSuggestBox>

                <!-- 统计. A toggle, because the panel it opens stays up until it is closed again: it is
                     read while something is going wrong, and a readout that vanished when the chrome
                     hid itself would be gone exactly when it was being watched. -->
                <ToggleButton
                    x:Name="StatsButton"
                    Background="Transparent"
                    BorderThickness="0"
                    Content="统计"
                    CornerRadius="6"
                    FontFamily="{StaticResource EgUiFontFamily}"
                    IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.StatsOpen, Mode=TwoWay}"
                    Padding="10,6"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="播放统计" />

                <ToggleButton
                    x:Name="PinButton"
                    Background="Transparent"
                    BorderThickness="0"
                    Click="OnTogglePin"
                    CornerRadius="6"
                    Padding="10,6"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="窗口置顶（T）">
                    <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE718;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
                </ToggleButton>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- 最小化 / 最大化 / 关闭. Real client-area buttons, because playback removes WS_CAPTION so the
                 picture can reach the top edge — Windows draws no caption buttons to inherit. Flush to the
                 corner and 32 tall, which is where the hand already expects them. 最大化 goes away in
                 fullscreen: the window's edges are the monitor's there, so the button could only do
                 nothing. -->
            <StackPanel
                x:Name="WindowButtons"
                Grid.Column="3"
                Orientation="Horizontal"
                VerticalAlignment="Top">
                <Button
                    x:Name="MinimizeButton"
                    Click="OnMinimizeWindow"
                    Background="Transparent"
                    BorderThickness="0"
                    Padding="0"
                    Width="46"
                    Height="32"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="最小化">
                    <FontIcon
                        FontSize="10"
                        Foreground="#FFF2F4F7"
                        Glyph="&#xE921;"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Button>
                <Button
                    x:Name="MaximizeButton"
                    Click="OnToggleMaximizeWindow"
                    Background="Transparent"
                    BorderThickness="0"
                    Padding="0"
                    Width="46"
                    Height="32"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="最大化或还原">
                    <FontIcon
                        x:Name="MaximizeGlyph"
                        FontSize="10"
                        Foreground="#FFF2F4F7"
                        Glyph="&#xE922;"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Button>
                <Button
                    x:Name="CloseButton"
                    Click="OnCloseWindow"
                    Background="Transparent"
                    BorderThickness="0"
                    Padding="0"
                    Width="46"
                    Height="32"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="关闭">
                    <FontIcon
                        FontSize="10"
                        Foreground="#FFF2F4F7"
                        Glyph="&#xE8BB;"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>

        <!-- ================= 播放统计面板 =================
             Drawn here rather than by mpv's stats.lua, and not by choice: the bundled libmpv-2.dll is
             built without Lua, so the script that would have drawn it was never loaded. PlaybackStats
             owns which properties are read and what the rows say; this is where they land.

             Below the title strip and outside the reveal rule — the strip comes and goes with the
             pointer, and a panel that came and went with it could not be read. -->
        <Border
            x:Name="StatsPanel"
            HorizontalAlignment="Left"
            VerticalAlignment="Top"
            Margin="20,104,0,0"
            Padding="14,10"
            Background="#D91E2126"
            BorderBrush="#4DFFFFFF"
            BorderThickness="1"
            CornerRadius="10"
            IsHitTestVisible="False"
            Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.StatsVisibility, Mode=OneWay}">
            <Grid x:Name="StatsRows" ColumnSpacing="16" RowSpacing="3">
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            </Grid>
        </Border>

        <!-- ================= 右侧：音量条 =================
             Its own overlay rather than a slider inside the transport bar. The pointer reaches the
             right edge far more often than it reaches one particular button, and the requests were
             「鼠标滚轮调整音量时要显示音量条」 and then 「加大音量条的尺寸，显示方式改为淡入淡出，鼠标指针越接近
             右边的中心显示越明显」 — none of which a control living inside the bar could answer. It no
             longer comes up with the bar: 「显示进度条的时候不需要同步显示音量条」.

             Opacity rather than Visibility, and the only overlay here that works that way. The
             ScalarTransition below is what makes it a fade — an implicit transition, so PlayerPage's
             FadeRail assigns the strength the rule decided and the compositor spends 220 ms getting
             there, which keeps 「is the rail up」 readable as a property instead of as a frame of an
             animation. Starts at zero with hit testing off, because the shell builds this page long
             before anything plays and an invisible rail must not answer clicks meant for the picture. -->
        <Border
            x:Name="Rail"
            HorizontalAlignment="Right"
            VerticalAlignment="Center"
            Margin="0,0,22,0"
            Padding="10,18"
            Background="#E61E2126"
            BorderBrush="#59FFFFFF"
            BorderThickness="1"
            CornerRadius="28"
            Opacity="0"
            IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Border.OpacityTransition>
                <ScalarTransition Duration="0:0:0.22" />
            </Border.OpacityTransition>
            <StackPanel Spacing="10" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                <TextBlock
                    x:Name="VolumeText"
                    FontSize="16"
                    FontWeight="SemiBold"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                    Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.VolumeLabel, Mode=OneWay}" />

                <Slider
                    x:Name="VolumeSlider"
                    Height="240"
                    Width="44"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                    IsThumbToolTipEnabled="False"
                    Maximum="100"
                    Minimum="0"
                    Orientation="Vertical"
                    StepFrequency="1"
                    Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.Volume, Mode=TwoWay}" />

                <Button
                    x:Name="MuteButton"
                    Click="OnToggleMute"
                    Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}"
                    Padding="10"
                    MinWidth="44"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="静音（M）">
                    <FontIcon x:Name="MuteGlyph" Glyph="{x:Bind ViewModel.SoundGlyph, Mode=OneWay}" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" FontSize="18" />
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>

        <!-- ================= 跳过片头/片尾 ================= -->
        <Button
            x:Name="SkipButton"
            HorizontalAlignment="Right"
            VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
            Margin="0,0,28,148"
            Padding="16,10"
            Background="#E62E333B"
            BorderBrush="#66FFFFFF"
            BorderThickness="1"
            CornerRadius="20"
            Command="{x:Bind ViewModel.TakeSkipCommand}"
            Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.SkipVisibility, Mode=OneWay}">
            <StackPanel Spacing="6">
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                    <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE893;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
                    <TextBlock x:Name="SkipText" Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SkipCaption, Mode=OneWay}" />
                    <TextBlock x:Name="SkipTip" Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SkipTip, Mode=OneWay}" Foreground="#FF8B93A0" FontSize="{StaticResource EgCaptionFontSize}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- The offer's own fifteen seconds, drawn rather than merely counted: a button that is
                     about to lapse should look like one. SkipPrompt.Remaining runs 1 down to 0. -->
                <ProgressBar
                    x:Name="SkipCountdown"
                    Height="2"
                    Maximum="1"
                    Minimum="0"
                    Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.SkipRemaining, Mode=OneWay}"
                    Background="#26FFFFFF"
                    Foreground="#FF8B93A0" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Button>

        <!-- ================= 底部：进度与传输控制 ================= -->
        <Grid
            x:Name="Bar"
            VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
            Background="{StaticResource BottomScrim}"
            Padding="20,26,20,12"
            RowSpacing="2"
            Visibility="Collapsed">
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>

            <!-- 进度 -->
            <Grid ColumnSpacing="12">
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                <TextBlock
                    x:Name="PositionText"
                    FontFamily="Consolas,Cascadia Mono,Segoe UI"
                    Foreground="#FFF2F4F7"
                    Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.PositionClock, Mode=OneWay}"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center" />

                <Grid Grid.Column="1" x:Name="SeekTrack" VerticalAlignment="Center" SizeChanged="OnSeekTrackResized">
                    <!-- The buffered-ahead readout, behind the slider's own track rather than beside
                         it: two bars would have the user comparing positions instead of reading one. -->
                    <ProgressBar
                        x:Name="CacheBar"
                        Height="4"
                        Maximum="1"
                        Minimum="0"
                        Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.CacheFraction, Mode=OneWay}"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Background="#33FFFFFF"
                        Foreground="#59FFFFFF"
                        IsIndeterminate="False" />

                    <!-- 章节刻度. Between the cache bar and the slider so the thumb passes over the
                         marks rather than under them, and never hit-testable: a tick is a thing to aim
                         at with the slider, not a thing to click. -->
                    <Canvas
                        x:Name="ChapterTicks"
                        Height="12"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        IsHitTestVisible="False" />

                    <Slider
                        x:Name="SeekSlider"
                        Margin="0,-1,0,0"
                        Background="Transparent"
                        Maximum="1000"
                        Minimum="0"
                        StepFrequency="1"
                        ThumbToolTipValueConverter="{StaticResource SeekClockConverter}"
                        Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.SeekValue, Mode=TwoWay}" />
                </Grid>

                <TextBlock
                    Grid.Column="2"
                    x:Name="DurationText"
                    FontFamily="Consolas,Cascadia Mono,Segoe UI"
                    Foreground="#FFA5ADBA"
                    Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.DurationClock, Mode=OneWay}"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center" />
            </Grid>

            <!-- 控制
                 Ranked rather than evenly weighted, as the WinForms bar was: play in the middle at
                 twice the size, the two episode steps beside it, the pickers pushed right, and the
                 things nobody presses twice an hour inside ⚙. -->
            <Grid Grid.Row="1" Margin="0,4,0,0">
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="2" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                    <Button
                        x:Name="PreviousButton"
                        Command="{x:Bind ViewModel.PreviousEpisodeCommand}"
                        Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}"
                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="上一集"
                        Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.EpisodeControlsVisibility, Mode=OneWay}">
                        <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE892;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
                    </Button>
                    <Button
                        x:Name="PlayButton"
                        Command="{x:Bind ViewModel.TogglePauseCommand}"
                        Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}"
                        Padding="12,6"
                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="播放/暂停（空格）">
                        <FontIcon x:Name="PlayGlyph" Glyph="{x:Bind ViewModel.PlayPauseGlyph, Mode=OneWay}" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" FontSize="20" />
                    </Button>
                    <Button
                        x:Name="NextButton"
                        Command="{x:Bind ViewModel.NextEpisodeCommand}"
                        Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}"
                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="下一集"
                        Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.EpisodeControlsVisibility, Mode=OneWay}">
                        <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE893;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- What is actually being decoded — 「1080p · HEVC · 8.4 GB」. The middle of the bar is
                     the one place nothing else wants, and this is the question a viewer asks of a file
                     often enough to be worth answering without opening a dialog for it. -->
                <TextBlock
                    Grid.Column="1"
                    x:Name="SourceText"
                    Foreground="#FFA5ADBA"
                    FontSize="{StaticResource EgCaptionFontSize}"
                    MaxLines="1"
                    Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SourceLabel, Mode=OneWay}"
                    TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center" />

                <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="2" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                    <Button
                        x:Name="EpisodeButton"
                        Content="选集"
                        Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}"
                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="本季剧集"
                        Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.EpisodeControlsVisibility, Mode=OneWay}">
                        <Button.Flyout>
                            <MenuFlyout x:Name="EpisodeMenu" Placement="Top" Opening="OnEpisodeMenuOpening" />
                        </Button.Flyout>
                    </Button>

                    <Button x:Name="AudioButton" Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}" ToolTipService.ToolTip="音轨">
                        <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE8D6;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
                        <Button.Flyout>
                            <MenuFlyout x:Name="AudioMenu" Placement="Top" Opening="OnAudioMenuOpening" />
                        </Button.Flyout>
                    </Button>

                    <Button x:Name="SubtitleButton" Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}" ToolTipService.ToolTip="字幕">
                        <FontIcon Glyph="&#xED1E;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
                        <Button.Flyout>
                            <MenuFlyout x:Name="SubtitleMenu" Placement="Top" Opening="OnSubtitleMenuOpening" />
                        </Button.Flyout>
                    </Button>

                    <Button x:Name="SpeedButton" Content="{x:Bind ViewModel.SpeedLabel, Mode=OneWay}" Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}" ToolTipService.ToolTip="播放速度">
                        <Button.Flyout>
                            <MenuFlyout x:Name="SpeedMenu" Placement="Top" Opening="OnSpeedMenuOpening" />
                        </Button.Flyout>
                    </Button>

                    <Button x:Name="MoreButton" Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}" ToolTipService.ToolTip="更多">
                        <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE713;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
                        <Button.Flyout>
                            <MenuFlyout x:Name="MoreMenu" Placement="Top" Opening="OnMoreMenuOpening" />
                        </Button.Flyout>
                    </Button>

                    <Button
                        x:Name="FullscreenButton"
                        Click="OnToggleFullscreen"
                        Style="{StaticResource OsdButtonStyle}"
                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="全屏（F）">
                        <FontIcon x:Name="FullscreenGlyph" Glyph="&#xE740;" Style="{StaticResource OsdGlyphStyle}" />
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>
            </Grid>
        </Grid>

        <!-- ================= 浮层收起时的细进度线 =================
             Two pixels at the very bottom edge, shown only while the chrome is hidden: with the bar
             gone there is nothing on screen that says how far in we are, and the answer is worth two
             pixels. Not hit-testable — reaching for it reveals the real bar, which is the thing that
             can be dragged. Inverse of Bar's visibility, so the two are never both up. -->
        <ProgressBar
            x:Name="ThinLine"
            Height="2"
            Maximum="1"
            Minimum="0"
            Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.ThinFraction, Mode=OneWay}"
            VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
            Background="#26FFFFFF"
            Foreground="#FFE0E4EA"
            IsHitTestVisible="False"
            Visibility="Collapsed" />

        <!-- ================= 暂停/播放提示 =================
             「暂停后显示一秒暂停图标就行（开启播放也弄个一秒的动画），别什么进度条标题音量条都持久显示在
             画面上」. Pausing used to pin the whole chrome — bar, title strip and volume rail — for as long
             as the file stayed paused, on the reasoning that a frozen frame has nothing to watch so the way
             out should stay visible. But 「the way out」 is one bit of information, and three overlays is not
             how you spell it: they cover the frame the pause was called to look at. So the pin is gone (see
             OnStatusApplied) and this is what says it instead — one glyph, in the middle, for a second.

             The one animation in this file, and the exception to the header's 「no storyboards anywhere」.
             That rule is about reveals the pointer asks for: a control you are already reaching for must be
             there the instant you arrive, and a fade only delays it. This is the opposite kind of thing —
             nobody is reaching for it, it appears and leaves on its own, and 「弄个一秒的动画」 is the request.
             A badge that simply blinked on and off for a second would read as a glitch; growing and fading
             reads as an acknowledgement.

             Not hit-testable, and starts collapsed with zero opacity so a layout pass before the first
             pause cannot flash it.

             「不要黑色的圆形边框，只要白色的三角形就可以，然后再放大一些」: the dark plate and its hairline
             ring are gone, and what is left is the glyph itself at three and a half times the size it was
             inside the circle. The only thing behind it is a second copy of the same glyph, black and a
             little larger — a rim that hugs the shape rather than a plate the shape sits on, because a
             white triangle over a white wall is otherwise not there at all. -->
        <Border
            x:Name="PulseBadge"
            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
            VerticalAlignment="Center"
            IsHitTestVisible="False"
            Opacity="0"
            RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5"
            Visibility="Collapsed">
            <Border.RenderTransform>
                <ScaleTransform x:Name="PulseScale" ScaleX="1" ScaleY="1" />
            </Border.RenderTransform>
            <Grid>
                <FontIcon
                    x:Name="PulseRim"
                    FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets"
                    FontSize="152"
                    Foreground="#59000000"
                    Glyph="&#xE769;" />
                <FontIcon
                    x:Name="PulseGlyph"
                    FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets"
                    FontSize="140"
                    Foreground="#FFFFFFFF"
                    Glyph="&#xE769;" />
            </Grid>
        </Border>
        <!-- ================= 章节缩略图 =================
             Emby's own chapter still for wherever the pointer is over the seek bar. The server drew
             these when it scanned the file, so this is a cache read rather than a decode — mpv cannot
             be asked for a frame it is not currently showing without seeking to it, and seeking to
             every pixel the pointer crosses is not a preview.

             A server that extracted no chapter images has none to send, and quite a few do not: the
             extraction is off by default on some builds and skipped for some containers. So the picture
             is collapsed rather than left as an empty frame — 「预览没有画面」 was a 212×119 hole with a
             chapter name under it — and what is left is an honest chip: which chapter, and the moment
             the pointer is on.

             Each of the three lines stands on its own, because a file can be missing any of them. No
             chapter marks at all — which is a whole class of server, not an edge case — leaves the time
             by itself, and that is still worth showing: the slider's own tooltip appears only while the
             thumb is being dragged, so hovering the bar would otherwise read as nothing at all.

             Positioned in code: Left/Top alignment plus a TranslateTransform the page sets from
             SeekTrack's own position, which is the only way the popup can sit above the bar without
             this file knowing how tall the bar happens to be. -->
        <Border
            x:Name="ChapterPeek"
            HorizontalAlignment="Left"
            VerticalAlignment="Top"
            Padding="4"
            Background="#F21E2126"
            BorderBrush="#59FFFFFF"
            BorderThickness="1"
            CornerRadius="8"
            IsHitTestVisible="False"
            Visibility="Collapsed">
            <Border.RenderTransform>
                <TranslateTransform x:Name="ChapterPeekOffset" />
            </Border.RenderTransform>
            <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                <Image
                    x:Name="ChapterImage"
                    Source="{x:Bind ViewModel.ChapterStill, Mode=OneWay}"
                    Width="212"
                    Height="119"
                    Stretch="UniformToFill"
                    Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.ChapterStillVisibility, Mode=OneWay}" />
                <TextBlock
                    x:Name="ChapterCaption"
                    FontSize="{StaticResource EgCaptionFontSize}"
                    Foreground="#FFE0E4EA"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                    MaxLines="1"
                    MaxWidth="212"
                    Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.ChapterCaption, Mode=OneWay}"
                    TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                    Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.ChapterCaptionVisibility, Mode=OneWay}" />

                <!-- The hovered moment. The slider's own thumb tooltip only appears while the thumb is
                     being dragged, so hovering the track had no time readout at all. -->
                <TextBlock
                    x:Name="ChapterClock"
                    FontFamily="Consolas,Cascadia Mono,Segoe UI"
                    FontSize="{StaticResource EgCaptionFontSize}"
                    Foreground="#FFA5ADBA"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                    Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.ChapterClock, Mode=OneWay}" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>

        <!-- ================= 换集时的遮挡层 =================
             Requirement 12. The video surface and mpv's child inside it both stay alive across an
             episode change, which is what stops the window from collapsing and rebuilding — but it
             also means the last frame of the finished episode sits there while mpv tears down one
             file and opens the next at whatever size and format it turns out to be. Nothing is wrong
             with the decode; it is simply nobody's job to have painted over it. This is that job.

             Opaque, and above everything else in the grid, so it cannot lose the race the WinForms
             cover kept losing. -->
        <Grid x:Name="Cover" Background="#FF0C0E11" Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.CoverVisibility, Mode=OneWay}">
            <StackPanel HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" Spacing="16">
                <ProgressRing IsActive="True" Width="40" Height="40" />
                <TextBlock x:Name="CoverText" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Foreground="#FFA5ADBA" Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.CoverMessage, Mode=OneWay}" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
